{"id":"en-151","title":"Control Card Replacement Guide for Laser Machines","family":"x-series","topic":"guides","read_minutes":2,"source_url":"https://wiki.1laser.com/en/x-series/control-card-replacement","source_updated_at":"2026-01-28T02:50:48.823Z","body_html":"<div><h2 id=\"control-card-replacement\"> Control Card Replacement</h2><div>\n\n</div><p>\n  This guide provides a <strong>step-by-step walkthrough for control card replacement</strong> \n  in laser machines. It covers safety precautions, required tools, enclosure removal, \n  control board disassembly, proper cable handling, and reinstallation to ensure stable \n  operation and prevent wiring errors.\n</p><div>\n\n</div><h2 id=\"note\"> Note:</h2>\n<p>\n  Before unplugging the cable, please take a photo to record the connection status \n  to prevent incorrect wiring during reinstallation.\n</p>\n<p>Keep the removed screws in a safe place to prevent loss.</p><div>\n\n</div><h2 id=\"tools-required\"> Tools Required</h2>\n<p>Hex wrenches (M2 &amp; M3), Phillips screwdriver</p><div>\n\n</div><figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/x-series/control-card-replacement/control-card-replacement_1.jpg\" alt=\"Tools required for laser control card replacement\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\">\n</figure><div>\n\n</div><h2 id=\"h-1-removing-the-machine-enclosure\"> 1. Removing the Machine Enclosure</h2><div>\n\n</div><p>① Ensure that the device power is disconnected.</p>\n<p>\n  ② Use the M2 hex wrench to remove the screws on the rear cover, \n  then take off the cover.\n</p><div>\n\n</div><figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/x-series/control-card-replacement/control-card-replacement_2.jpg\" alt=\"Removing rear cover screws from laser machine enclosure\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\">\n</figure><div>\n\n</div><p>③ Remove the screws on the right-side panel.</p><div>\n\n</div><figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/x-series/control-card-replacement/control-card-replacement_3.jpg\" alt=\"Removing right-side panel screws on laser machine\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\">\n</figure><div>\n\n</div><figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/x-series/control-card-replacement/control-card-replacement_4.jpg\" alt=\"Right-side panel partially removed from laser machine\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\">\n</figure><div>\n\n</div><p>④ Before removing the right-side panel, disconnect the following cables:</p>\n<ul>\n  <li>Emergency stop switch power cable</li>\n  <li>Touchscreen signal cable</li>\n  <li>PM2.5 detector power cable</li>\n</ul><div>\n\n</div><figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/x-series/control-card-replacement/control-card-replacement_5.jpg\" alt=\"Disconnecting internal cables before removing side panel\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\">\n</figure><div>\n\n</div><h2 id=\"h-2-removing-the-tl-time-control-board\"> 2. Removing the TL-time Control Board</h2><div>\n\n</div><p>① Disconnect the connectors shown in the image.</p><div>\n\n</div><figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/x-series/control-card-replacement/control-card-replacement_6.jpg\" alt=\"Disconnecting connectors from TL-time control board\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\">\n</figure><div>\n\n</div><p>\n  ② Remove the two network cables from the switch. \n  Label the cables before removing them as shown in the image.\n</p><div>\n\n</div><figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/x-series/control-card-replacement/control-card-replacement_7.jpg\" alt=\"Removing and labeling network cables from control board\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\">\n</figure><div>\n\n</div><p>\n  ③ Remove the two screws shown in the image. \n  This will allow you to move the TL-time control board aside.\n</p><div>\n\n</div><figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/x-series/control-card-replacement/control-card-replacement_8.jpg\" alt=\"Removing mounting screws from TL-time control board\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\">\n</figure><div>\n\n</div><h2 id=\"h-3-replacing-the-control-board\"> 3. Replacing the Control Board</h2><div>\n\n</div><h3 id=\"removing-the-old-control-board\"> Removing the Old Control Board</h3><div>\n\n</div><p>① Disconnect all cables from the control board.</p><div>\n\n</div><figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/x-series/control-card-replacement/control-card-replacement_9.jpg\" alt=\"Disconnecting cables from laser control board\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\">\n</figure><div>\n\n</div><p>② Use a screwdriver to remove the four screws securing the control board.</p><div>\n\n</div><figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/x-series/control-card-replacement/control-card-replacement_10.jpg\" alt=\"Removing screws securing laser control board\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\">\n</figure><div>\n\n</div><h3 id=\"installing-the-new-control-board\"> Installing the New Control Board</h3><div>\n\n</div><p>① Remove the outer casing of the control board using a Phillips screwdriver.</p><div>\n\n</div><figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/x-series/control-card-replacement/control-card-replacement_11.jpg\" alt=\"Removing protective casing from new control board\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\">\n</figure><div>\n\n</div><p>② Secure the new control board to the enclosure and reconnect all cables.</p>\n<p>\n  <strong>Note:</strong> Do not miss any connectors. \n  (The image shows an incorrect connection with a missing terminal.)\n</p><div>\n\n</div><figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/x-series/control-card-replacement/control-card-replacement_12.jpg\" alt=\"Incorrect control board wiring showing missing terminal\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\">\n</figure><div>\n\n</div><h2 id=\"h-4-reassembling-the-machine\"> 4. Reassembling the Machine</h2><div>\n\n</div><p>\n  Restore the TL-time control board, switch, and enclosure to their original positions, \n  following the connections made before disassembly.\n</p>\n</div>","headings":[{"level":1,"id":"control-card-replacement","text":"Control Card Replacement"},{"level":2,"id":"note","text":"Note:"},{"level":2,"id":"tools-required","text":"Tools Required"},{"level":2,"id":"h-1-removing-the-machine-enclosure","text":"1. Removing the Machine Enclosure"},{"level":2,"id":"h-2-removing-the-tl-time-control-board","text":"2. Removing the TL-time Control Board"},{"level":2,"id":"h-3-replacing-the-control-board","text":"3. Replacing the Control Board"},{"level":3,"id":"removing-the-old-control-board","text":"Removing the Old Control Board"},{"level":3,"id":"installing-the-new-control-board","text":"Installing the New Control Board"},{"level":2,"id":"h-4-reassembling-the-machine","text":"4. Reassembling the Machine"}],"technical_version":"unknown"}